   - GHOST KEYS — ROOT CAUSE FOUND AND FIXED: it was our own
     canlinux-input-watchdog. Every 4 seconds it injected
     `xdotool key XF86Ungrab` into the live session UNCONDITIONALLY; on this
     keymap XF86Ungrab is level 7 of keycode 106, so xdotool synthesizes
     Ctrl+Alt+KP_Divide through the XTEST virtual keyboard. A synthetic
     Ctrl+Alt landing on whatever key the user was typing at that instant IS
     the reported "hotkeys open launchpad, screenshot, all sorts of
     applications with no user intention" (Ctrl+Alt+A = screenshot, etc.).
     Recorded live with the new recorder: device 5 "Virtual core XTEST
     keyboard", keycodes 37/64/106, six events within 1 ms, every ~4 s, with
     nobody at the machine. The watchdog now ungrabs ONLY a grab that has been
     stuck for 15 s and ONLY while the user has been idle for 1.5 s (a real
     XGrabKeyboard/XGrabPointer test + XScreenSaver idle time), and the
     service is restarted on the fixed code during install.
   - RDP WORKS AGAIN. FreeRDP rejects /smart-sizing and /dynamic-resolution
     TOGETHER ("mutually exclusive options") and exits before dialing; the
     1.5.3 resize/fullscreen change shipped both, so every RDP launch from
     1.5.3 to 1.5.7 died instantly (1.5.2 shipped neither and worked). The
     two are now alternatives: /dynamic-resolution by default (live resize on
     Windows 10/11 and modern xrdp), ONE automatic retry with /smart-sizing
     if the client refuses it, fullscreen (/f) and auto-reconnect unchanged,
     and a unit check that fails the build if both flags ever share one argv.
   - "Open log file" OPENS THE LOG: it was xdg-open with every error thrown
     away, and text/x-log resolves to a word processor on this desktop. It
     now uses the first real text viewer that exists and spawns (deepin-editor
     first) and says which one — or exactly why none could.
   - WIRELESS TOGGLE NEXT TO ITS TITLE: the 1.5.1 widening of the network
