  One-command cumulative Service Pack 1 installer for Fihri OS 1.0 systems
  (1.4.0 adds the Calendar service idempotency fix and the laptop Fn /
  function-key support on top of the verified 1.2.0 P1B batch —
  CANDIDATE / UNVERIFIED, not published):
    0. Installs dde-calendar 5.9.1-4build2+canlinux1 (parity defect #22):
       the dde-calendar-service ColorType/JobType seed is idempotent
       (INSERT OR IGNORE), so the per-activation "UNIQUE constraint failed"
       flood disappears while every existing row and all user data are
       preserved. The .deb is staged from a LOCAL pool only (it is never
       fetched from the network), SHA-256 verified against a pinned hash,
       and installed dependency-driven through apt/dpkg; this package never
       edits, deletes or migrates the calendar database.
   0b. Installs canlinux-laptop-hotkeys 1.0.1 (GENERIC, every laptop): the
       backlight udev rule for EVERY /sys/class/backlight device and EVERY
       *kbd_backlight* LED (mode 0660 root:video, ACTION=="add" only, so it
       can never re-grant a permission the RDP privacy lock just revoked),
       the canlinux-kbd-backlight helper (bounded +/-25 step, clamped to
       max_brightness, silent no-op without a keyboard-backlight LED), the
       clearing of the three DEAD kbd-brightness GSettings grabs of
       dde-session-daemon 6.0.43 and the XF86KbdBrightness* custom
       shortcut. The payload is staged from a LOCAL pool only (never fetched
       from the network), SHA-256 verified against a pinned hash and
       installed with an exact final-version gate. 1.0.1 fixes the D1 defect
       of 1.0.0: the shortcut fragment is shipped under the exact name the
       postinst merges (/usr/share/canlinux-laptop-hotkeys/custom.ini), so
       the XF86KbdBrightness* keys are really bound now; the postinst
       verifies the merge and fails loudly when it did not take effect. The panel-brightness
       (mon-brightness-*) and all audio/media bindings are NOT touched and
       NO Apple-specific remap is installed.
   0d. Installs dde-file-manager 6.0.55-2+canlinux1 (parity defect #23 /
       storage G5): the backport of the upstream fix "refactor: remove file
       data caching system" (linuxdeepin commit 726d127, first released in
       6.5.133 and present in the 6.6.x line of the golden reference VM).
       RootInfo::startWork() no longer takes the cache early-return that
       suppressed the directory traversal, the running traversal thread is
       no longer disconnected + replaced (which cancelled the in-flight
       enumeration and permanently poisoned the root), and a
       registered-but-empty prehandler no longer swallows the initial
       fetch. Fixes "Folder is empty" on populated local folders, drives
       and USB media. The .deb is staged from a LOCAL pool only (never
       fetched from the network), SHA-256 verified against a pinned hash,
       installed with dpkg and held. User files and bookmarks are never
       touched.
   0c. Installs fihri-macbook-support 1.2.2 on APPLE HARDWARE ONLY
       (MacBook Pro 10,1 and friends): fnmode=1 (macOS-like, OPERATOR DECISION
       2026-11-17: the F-row directly gives the special brightness /
       keyboard-backlight / Mission Control / Launchpad / media functions,
       Fn+F-row gives plain F1..F12) and the
       Apple-scoped XF86LaunchA (Mission Control) / XF86LaunchB (Launchpad)
       bindings. It is deliberately NOT a Depends/Recommends of this package,
       so apt never puts an Apple package on a non-Apple machine: the
       applier stages and installs it only after the hardware gate
       (fihri-hw-detect --is-macbook, or the exact DMI gate) proved Apple
       hardware, again from a LOCAL pool only and SHA-256 verified. On
       non-Apple hardware nothing is staged, nothing is installed, no fnmode
       is written and no LaunchA/LaunchB binding is created; when the
       hardware detection is unavailable the Apple payload is skipped
       loudly, the state is recorded as UNVERIFIED and the generic SP1
       continues. The RDP session-owner flow is UNCHANGED: neither package
       ships, installs, replaces or restarts canlinux-session-owner.
